  "notes": "WP1 reference design: TPS563201, L_4R7_SRN4018 (4.7uH), 2x C_10u_25V_1206_X7R_IN input caps (one 10uF/25V cap alone gives only 7.0uF effective at 8.4V, below the 10uF datasheet minimum -- see docs/CATALOG.md section 3 -- two in parallel give 14.0uF), 2x C_22u_10V_0805_X5R_OUT output caps, C_100n_50V_0603_X7R_BST bootstrap cap, R0603:33k2/R0603:10k feedback divider (TI Table 7-2 values), R0603:68k1/R0603:27k4 EN divider (chosen so EN crosses VENH(min)=1.6V already by VIN=5.58V, safely below the 6.4V discharged-battery floor; R_EN1=100k/R_EN2=27k from the pre-WP1 harness would only turn on above 7.44V, which is why they changed)."
